{"id":"word:hebrew:H816","type":"word","title":"אָשַׁם","subtitle":"H816 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be guilty ; by implication to be punished or perish","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אָשַׁם (H816) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 35 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אָשַׁם (ʼâsham) means to be guilty ; by implication to be punished or perish First listed occurrence: 2Chr 19 10."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אָשַׁם","transliteration":"ʼâsham","pronunciation":"aw-sham'","strong":"H816","lemmaId":"hebrew:H816","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וְ/אָשֵֽׁם","יֶאְשַׁ֖ם","יֶאְשָׁ֔מוּ","וְ/אָשֵׁ֖ם","יֶאְשְׁמוּ֙"],"morphs":[["HVqi3mp",7],["HC/Vqq3ms",7],["HVqi2mp",2],["HC/Vqw3mp",2],["HVqa",2],["HVqp3ms",2],["HC/Vqi3mp",1],["HVqp2fs",1],["HC/Vqp3ms",1],["HVqj3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be guilty ; by implication to be punished or perish","usage":"× certainly, be(-come, made) desolate, destroy, × greatly, be(-come, found, hold) guilty, offend (acknowledge offence), trespass.","full":"H816. asham אָשֵׁם אָשַׁם, verb offend, be guilty (Arabic , id. , sin, offence , , , requital, fault, guilt, mulct , compare Ethiopic ) — אָשַׁם Lev 5:19 ; Num 5:7 ; אָשֵׁם Hab 1:11 7 t.; אָֽשְׁמָה Num 5:6 ; אָשָׁ֑מְתָּ Prov 30:10 ; אָשַׁמְתְּ Ezek 22:4 ; אָשֵׁ֑מוּ Lev 4:13 ; Imperfect יֶאְשַׁם Hosea 4:15 13 t.; Infinitive absolute אָשֹׁם Lev 5:19 ; אָשׁוֺם Ezek 25:12 ; &#8212; 1 commit an offence, a trespass, do a wrong , or an injury , with ׃לְ ליהוה אָשַׁם אָשֹׁם he hath done a great wrong to Yahweh (in violating the commands) Lev 5:19 (P); לוֺ אָשַׁם לַאֲשֶׁר וְנָתַן and he shall give it (restitution) to him to whom he did wrong Num 5:7 (P), compare 2Chr 19:10 (twice in verse); אָשׁוֺם וַיֶאְשְׁמוּ and they committed lasting wrong (irreparable wrong, the Edomites against Judah) Ezek 25:12 . 2 be or become guilty Judg 21:22 ; Jer 50:7 ; Hosea 4:15 ; Hab 1:11 ; in offences requiring sin-offering Lev 4:13 , 22 , 27 (P), of trespass-offering 5:2-3 , 17 ; Leviticus 5:23; Num 5:6 (P); with ל guilty of Lev 5:4-5 , (P), with ב in or through Ezek 22:4 ; Hosea 13:1 . 3 be held guilty, bear punishment Psa 34:22 ; Psalm 34:23; Prov 30:10 ; Isa 24:6 ; Jer 2:3 ; Hosea 5:15 ; 10:2 ; 14:1 ; Zech 11:5 ; Ezek 6:6 (but compare שָׁמֵם ). Niph`al נֶאְשָׁמוּ suffer punishment Joel 1:18 (si vera lectio; Me We and others נָשַׁמּוּ , √ שׁמם , compare Dr on the passage ). Hiph`il Imperfect suffix הַאֲשִׁימֵם declare them guilty Psa 5:11 .","rootNote":"or אָשֵׁם ; a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Chr 19 10","keyReferences":["2Chr 19 10","2Chr 19 10","Ezek 6 6","Ezek 22 4","Ezek 25 12","Ezek 25 12","Hab 1 11","Hos 4 15"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":35,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Chr 19 10","book":"2Chr","chapter":19,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יֶאְשְׁמוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3mp"},{"reference":"2Chr 19 10","book":"2Chr","chapter":19,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תֶאְשָֽׁמוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2mp"},{"reference":"Ezek 6 6","book":"Ezek","chapter":6,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יֶאְשְׁמ֜וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqi3mp"},{"reference":"Ezek 22 4","book":"Ezek","chapter":22,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אָשַׁ֗מְתְּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp2fs"},{"reference":"Ezek 25 12","book":"Ezek","chapter":25,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יֶּאְשְׁמ֥וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"Ezek 25 12","book":"Ezek","chapter":25,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אָשׁ֖וֹם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqa"},{"reference":"Hab 1 11","book":"Hab","chapter":1,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אָשֵׁ֑ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqp3ms"},{"reference":"Hos 4 15","boo